From: Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Wait for the APM callback and keep codec capture on jackless boards

APR installs the service callback after probe returns: querying synchronously
inside apm_probe cannot receive its response. Publish only a successfully probed
APM, check that its callback is installed, and query on demand. Serialize its
lifetime with readiness calls, propagate transport errors, handle BASIC replies
without inventing readiness, and validate the four-byte SPF response.

GET_SPF_STATE has no APM payload header. Ready/not-ready are 1/0, per AudioReach:
https://github.com/AudioReach/audioreach-engine/blob/5773bf8e627c9857481dd338a9ec4aea4a49afd3/fwk/api/apm/apm_api.h

The existing liuqin DTS documents analog onboard microphones and no headset
jack. Opt this board out of analog jack/impedance detection while retaining
codec controls, SoundWire DAIs, microphone and speaker paths. Other boards keep
the existing jack behavior. A missing optional DMIC rate retains divider 2.
No firmware, calibration, clock/voltage tables, DRM or USB role policy changes.

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,wcd938x.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,wcd938x.yaml
index ab1c6285d..b4f6a8fa1 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,wcd938x.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,wcd938x.yaml
@@ -23,6 +23,12 @@ properties:
       - qcom,wcd9380-codec
       - qcom,wcd9385-codec
 
+  qcom,mbhc-disabled:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      Disable analog headset jack detection on boards with no such connector.
+      Codec playback and microphone capture interfaces remain available.
+
   mux-controls:
     description: A reference to the audio mux switch for
       switching CTIA/OMTP Headset types
